;; Arc 251 stone 251.8d-ii — ⛔ GATE E NON-VACUITY, KEYWORD SPELLING.
;;
;; 251.8d-ii taught the Gate E binder scan that a param ANNOTATION's type is not a
;; binder name (`[~cv :- wat.gen/Coord]`). This file is the row that proves the cure
;; did NOT loosen what the gate inspects: a template that introduces a REAL literal
;; name in `fn` binder position is still refused, with the located binder `y`.
;;
;; Its symbol-spelled twin is `probe_arc251_8d_hygiene_fn_binder_symbol.wat.bad`;
;; the two files differ ONLY in the spelling of the fn head, the annotation arrows
;; and the type. Both must be refused, with the SAME binder.
;;
;; The body is an `if`, not a bare quasiquote, because `is_quasiquote_form` routes a
;; bare-quasiquote macro body PAST `validate_macro_definition` entirely (255.11 §4(a)
;; — the router is deliberately keyword-only). A quasiquote NESTED in a program body
;; is the reachable position for this gate.
(:wat::core::defmacro :my::capturing-param
  [x <- :wat::WatAST]
  -> :wat::WatAST
  (:wat::core::if (:wat::core::= 1 1)
    `((:wat::core::fn [y <- :wat::core::i64] -> :wat::core::i64 y) ~x)
    `~x))
(:wat::core::defn :user::probe [n <- :wat::core::i64]
  -> :wat::core::i64 (:my::capturing-param n))
